### Response Parameters

{% include '_generic_v4_response.md.j2' %}

#### data

| Field | Type | Never null | Description |
|-------|------|------------|-------------|
| id | long | Yes | Cron job ID; a newly generated ID when creating, and the same as the `id` in the request when updating |
| name | string | No | Cron job name |
| status | int | Yes | Cron job status. Options: 1 (enabled), 0 (disabled). Saving does not change this state: creating always returns 0, while updating returns the state the cron job had before the update |
